WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.000
We are now approved in 65 countries outside of the U.S.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:08.620
In Japan, we've already reached first-line NBRX leadership, as you can see in the lower chart.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:13.460
In Germany, our early NBRX first-line share is already up to 15%.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.460
So we're very excited for the trajectory of Semblix and to continue to be a growth driver

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.580
long into the future.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.700
Now, with Cosentix, we had a solid quarter, 10% constant currency growth,

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.940
in part driven by some one-timers, but still strong underlying growth.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.980
And when you look at in the U.S., we were up 16%.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:39.640
You can see that in HS, we're steady in our NBRX share in the high 40s,

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:46.020
and we expect that to continue. We see steady demand growth in HS and IV.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.760
Underlying growth in the U.S. is around the mid-single digits, as we've guided to in the past.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:52.000
And I would like to thank all of you for joining us today.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.680
Outside of the U.S., continued solid growth.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:59.500
In Europe, we do see additional challenges in China with more competition,

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:04.000
but we're able to manage that to maintain the overall global performance of the brand.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:10.720
And then we're excited by the Phase 3 replenish PMR, polymyalgia rheumatica data,

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.720
which we recently published and presented at UR.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.180
It showed very strong data with sustained remission at 52 weeks.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.960
That was twice as high in patients treated with Cosentix versus placebo.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.440
So we're anticipating FDA approval for that indication in the second half

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:32.640
and remain on track for the $8 billion peak sales guidance that we've previously provided.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:40.260
Now moving to slide 13, Rapsido continues its strong launch trajectory with Phase 3 SINDU data

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.340
now available to support our broader potential in urticaria.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:51.980
First targeting, starting with the CSU launch, we see continued solid U.S. uptake over 4,000 units.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.700
Over 10,000 prescribers, over 10,000 patients treated.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.040
60% of those patients are treated in the first-line setting.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.320
We see steady expansion in our patient access.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:09.660
We have two of the three major PBMs now covering remibrutinib, Rapsido, with PA at a label.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.740
And in the second half, we expect steady expansion in that access

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:17.540
with an effective bridge and sample program in place.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.520
We don't expect an inflection per se.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.160
We think this will be steady expansion.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:21.980
We want to ensure.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.880
We're disciplined in how we approach getting reimbursement,

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.520
given the multiple indications we hope to secure for remibrutinib over time.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.520
Outside of the U.S., we see good traction in China.

